id: pm-rust-crash-harness
title: Compare native and published crash recovery with a reusable kill corpus
description: "Reusable TypeScript process-kill/restart differential SDK and command against the locked published oracle; compare acknowledged durable bytes, append-only histories and restart receipts on disposable plain-directory trackers."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: conformance,crash-consistency,harness
created_at: "2026-10-21T21:59:35.474Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T06:52:47.487Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Every declared crash boundary preserves acknowledged writes; failures retain minimized synthetic reproductions and never rewrite original history.; Typed SDK and CLI with bounded TOON/JSON receipts and actionable refusals; documented example; public tracker read-copy validation with measured counts; exact-head CI release-check passes.
blocked_by: pm-rust-cross-operation-journal
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-rust-cross-operation-journal,blocked_by,"2026-10-23T06:50:01.812Z",codex-agent,"cli:update:blocked_by",detected
comments[17]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T21:59:37.843Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: published CLI 2026.10.21 matches the locked oracle. Native tests cover normal command differentials and manually reconstructed durable journals; they do not run a reusable live kill/restart corpus. pm-ops assurance reports measurements; pm-vcs writer publication is backend-specific. This feature adds cross-implementation crash evidence beyond lock/parity work. Reconciliation PR 103 closures and performance PR 102 items are excluded. TypeScript-only SDK/command; synthetic failures; targeted local checks; full gate in CI."
  "2026-10-21T22:16:09.535Z",codex-agent,"Implemented the typed TypeScript SDK and standalone just crash CLI. Declared boundaries are all observed rename/fsync task-local ordinals: event-loop write calls were rejected as unstable storage boundaries after real tracing. Two mutation families run on disposable non-git clones; same-family restart checks exact durable bytes and raw per-runtime restart receipts, with explicit shared cross-runtime acknowledgement projections. Synthetic probing measured 20 real kills, 20 preserved acknowledged writes/history prefixes, two successful baseline byte/acknowledgement comparisons and two early native lock-initialization restart refusals. Those refusals are retained as minimal one-item synthetic cases; no original stream is repaired. Full runtime crash conformance is not claimed. Adding independent replay/no-git regressions and public-copy measurements before CI."
  "2026-10-21T22:19:48.804Z",codex-agent,"Read-only public-copy validation: public main c0154dbd7cd8071ac52b891be13f956f7a0f21fd, 74 items and 154 authoritative files in a non-git copy with read-only permissions. Measured 20 injected kills, 20 acknowledged-write preservations, 20 exact retained-history prefixes, two cross-runtime baseline byte/acknowledgement matches, 18 successful restart state/receipt checks, two independently reproduced native incomplete-lock restart refusals. Source fingerprint unchanged. Retained evidence is synthetic only. Follow-up pm-rust-crash-lock-restart covers the safe recovery policy, outside this harness change. Behavioral controls disabling history-prefix checking, exact inventory comparison and injected-kill admission each fail their targeted regression with exit 1 and pass after exact byte restoration."
  "2026-10-21T22:21:46.519Z",codex-agent,"Final targeted checks: pinned PM linked runner passes 14/14 Node regressions with no skips, including real native/published kills, read-only source-output guards, a PATH with no git executable, and independent one-case replay. Strict erasable TypeScript typecheck, ESLint, Rust fmt and targeted binary Clippy pass. Four behavioral negative controls now fail independently and pass after byte restoration, including rejecting a successful restart that lost its own history. Full unchanged-threshold Rust release-check is reserved for CI; no local full release suite was run. Local health retains existing guidance/provenance/stale-item advisories and shared configuration drift; history was not repaired. CI uses its existing clone-local configuration setup. Full CI run results and exact counts will be linked in the PR."
  "2026-10-22T10:38:52.442Z",codex-agent,"PR 104 review round: pulled remote head and merged origin/main. PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6vBg8Y is valid: oracle metadata read/parse errors bypass oracle_version. Adding public SDK/CLI regressions for missing, unreadable, malformed, invalid-shape and wrong-version metadata. Full-diff self-review found the same parse-before-typed-refusal pattern in mutation acknowledgements: malformed successful stdout bypasses baseline_failed. Covering and correcting that instance too. Replay-manifest parsing already has its typed invalid_options catch. Latest substantive CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. No thread replies or resolutions."
  "2026-10-22T10:42:18.350Z",codex-agent,"Full-diff validation review also found malformed source settings JSON bypassed its unsafe_source guard. Corrected all three parse-before-validation paths: oracle metadata maps to oracle_version, source settings to unsafe_source, and malformed successful mutation stdout to baseline_failed. Added ten SDK oracle metadata cases, bounded JSON/default CLI refusal checks, source immutability checks and a real published-CLI baseline with an incompatible executable. No PM SDK mocks; all fixtures are disposable non-git directories. Replay-manifest parsing already preserves invalid_options. Original histories and all gate thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-22T10:43:02.665Z",codex-agent,"Independent revert proofs complete with exact source-byte restoration. Oracle metadata: replacing only its guarded read/parse with the original statement makes both SDK and CLI regressions fail (2/2, io_error); restored both pass. Source settings: reverting only its guarded parse fails 1/1 with io_error; restored passes 1/1. Mutation acknowledgement: reverting only its guarded parse fails 1/1 with io_error; restored passes 1/1 using real published init/create processes and an incompatible native executable. Exact commands: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"oracle metadata\" scripts/crash-harness.test.mts; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"malformed source settings\" scripts/crash-harness.test.mts; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"malformed mutation acknowledgements\" scripts/crash-harness.test.mts. Each negative run exits 1 from the intended assertion; each restored run exits 0."
  "2026-10-22T10:44:51.308Z",codex-agent,"Final local targeted validation passed: strict erasable TypeScript compiler and ESLint checks; full crash harness 18/18 with zero skips; linked new regressions 4/4. All three independent behavior reverts failed exactly their intended assertions (2+1+1), then passed restored (2+1+1). Isolated pinned-PM health passed. Starting unchanged-threshold just release-check with the existing 35-minute release CI budget as the local wall-time bound."
  "2026-10-22T10:56:48.191Z",codex-agent,"Local full release attempt is incomplete, not failed: dependency install, fmt, strict Clippy and private-item rustdoc passed; the cold Rust test build was stopped under shared-host contention (main compiler about 7 percent CPU over six minutes). No compiler or test assertion failed. Using exact-head CI for the full unchanged-threshold release gate; this PR remains the active round until that gate passes. Targeted TypeScript compiler/lint checks, full Linux crash harness 18/18, linked new controls 4/4 and all independent revert proofs already pass."
  "2026-10-22T11:23:46.735Z",codex-agent,"Full CI release evidence at code head 5b84803625d18e3ab3b7fdb4454a49448a628bf6: Linux just release-check passed (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/actions/runs/39767043319/job/119784971422). Ordinary and instrumented Rust tests each passed 578 across 22 suites, zero failed or ignored; Rust lines 14025/14025, functions 1466/1466, regions 23438/23438, branches 3296/3296, all 100 percent. TypeScript compiler, ESLint and Linux crash harness 18/18 with zero skips also passed inside the gate. Audit, changelog and strict tracker health passed; only the pre-existing allowed RUSTSEC-2024-0449 advisory remains. macOS full release gate also passed: 567 ordinary and 567 instrumented Rust tests; all four required Rust metrics 100 percent; Node harness 11 passed with 7 declared Linux-only skips. The stopped local cold-build attempt is incomplete evidence; CI supplies the full pass. Releasing the claim and retaining in_progress for orchestrator verification. Final receipt-head CI evidence will be linked from PR 104; no thread replies/resolutions, PR merge or release."
  "2026-10-22T16:37:02.495Z",codex-agent,"New PR 104 review round: pulled remote head 328ff00, then merged origin/main a600bd8 because the branch was one commit behind. Thread PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6vRw2E is valid: the retained-case example claims every replay selects one implementation/syscall/ordinal, but baseline_parity evidence reruns its scenario across both implementations and all observed boundaries. The public SDK replay docstring has the same overstatement. Will correct both descriptions and add a regression tied to the replay contract with a documentation revert proof. Latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Existing implementation, completed review fixes and append-only histories remain intact."
  "2026-10-22T16:41:16.374Z",codex-agent,"Documentation revert proof for PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6vRw2E: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"replay guidance\" scripts/crash-harness.test.mts checks the public guide and SDK docstring. Reverting only docs/CRASH_HARNESS.md yields one intended missing-baseline_parity-exception failure and one unaffected pass. Restoring it and reverting only the replay API docstring yields the other intended failure and one unaffected pass. Both exact byte sequences restored: 2/2 pass. These are documentation-contract controls; runtime replay behavior was already correct and was not changed. The complete just crash-check passes strict erasable TypeScript, ESLint and 20/20 Linux tests with zero failed/canceled/skipped; current native build also passes. Pinned-PM linked controls pass 2/2; result storage remains disabled by project policy, so results are retained here."
  "2026-10-22T16:41:17.977Z",codex-agent,"Self-review of the whole PR confirms the only overstatements were the retained-case guide and public replay docstring; README, CLI help, manifest validation and the single-boundary selection type do not claim that every replay selects one case. Original histories, stored commands and implementation behavior remain untouched. Releasing the implementation claim with status retained in_progress. Final exact-head unchanged just release-check CI receipts and counts will be recorded in PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/104; pending CI is not approval. The original stacked-PR instruction still requires merging this completed update and main into PR 105 after PR 104 has passed and been pushed. No review replies/resolutions, PR merge or release."
  "2026-10-22T16:47:29.332Z",codex-agent,"Additional self-review caught an LF-only assumption in the new guide regression. The matcher now accepts both LF and CRLF and exercises both spellings using the real guide contents. Reverting only the optional carriage-return matcher makes the CRLF assertion fail; restoring it passes both guidance tests 2/2. Strict TypeScript and ESLint pass. No documentation, runtime function, input fixture or gate threshold changed in this follow-up. Superseded pending CI at 84ddc56 is not used as approval; the corrected final head needs fresh full release CI."
  "2026-10-23T06:38:11.820Z",codex-agent,"Orchestrator review follow-up on PR 104: remote f555a42 was current; merged main c46ad00 and preserved both benchmark and crash recipes in two overlap resolutions. Reusing this item, without redoing completed refusal/doc fixes. Will capture runtime journals, add cross-operation restart plus a return-to-original-operation probe, inject published history-open failures, compare recovered runtime outcomes, disclose clock semantics, keep replay unconditional, preserve measured failure when synthetic reduction refuses, and record reproducible source/toolchain/control artifacts. Native cross-operation repair remains a separate blocking defect unless safely implemented. No review replies or mentions."
  "2026-10-23T06:44:41.257Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed blocking cross-operation journal defect with real update rename-1 kill: restart comment exits 0 while journal persists, returning to update exits 2. Created pm-rust-cross-operation-journal as priority-0 blocking Issue linked to PR 104; no Rust recovery fix is folded into this TypeScript harness change. History-path openat injection also proves published item/history divergence with exit-0 restart. Historical 20-boundary receipts remain immutable and are no longer described as complete crash evidence."
  "2026-10-23T06:52:47.487Z",codex-agent,"Targeted validation now confirms update cross-operation replay and reduction-refusal CLI behavior, with clock disclosure assertions. Permanent manifests replace conditional replay coverage. Runtime snapshots retain canonical transaction JSON plus raw runtime frames; unpublished temporary files remain observed but are not misclassified as committed journals. Shared recovery comparisons fail on byte, receipt projection, state or pending-journal mismatches, and unpaired cuts are not counted. Next commit pins the code source for the reproducible control recorder; complete regressions and gate evidence remain pending."
